<div class="callout callout-info">
  <div class="callout-title">💡 About ChemBuddy</div>
  ChemBuddy by Prajwal A Kambar was engineered specifically to solve the unique academic pressures faced by postgraduate Chemistry students—balancing rigorous laboratory synthesis, spectroscopic characterization, competitive exam preparation (CSIR-NET, GATE, SET), and strict 75% attendance regulations.
</div>

<!-- CHAPTER 1 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>1. Introduction & Architecture Overview</h2>
<p>
  <strong>ChemBuddy</strong> is a comprehensive, offline-first mobile and desktop application designed exclusively for Master of Science (MSc) Chemistry students, researchers, and educators. Unlike generic student planners or basic scientific calculators, ChemBuddy brings together specialized chemoinformatics engines, textbook-grade spectroscopy analyzers, advanced attendance algorithms, and grounded artificial intelligence in a unified, private, and distraction-free interface.
</p>

<h3>Design Philosophy & Core Pillars</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>100% Offline Core Functionality:</strong> Attendance calculations, timetable parsing, 16 chemistry calculators, Woodward-Hoffmann selection rules, spectroscopy databases, reaction prediction, and 2D vector SVG generation execute entirely on-device with zero internet connection required.</li>
  <li><strong>Scientific Rigor:</strong> All formulas, mechanisms, spectroscopic peaks, and unit conversions follow IUPAC standards and standard graduate textbooks (Silverstein, Pavia, March, Clayden, Carey-Sundberg).</li>
  <li><strong>Privacy & Local Ownership:</strong> Student profiles, attendance logs, notes, and PDF documents are stored locally in high-performance encrypted Hive boxes. Cloud synchronization via Supabase is completely optional.</li>
  <li><strong>Laboratory Ergonomics:</strong> The dark-mode interface (`AppColors` design system: #0A0914 canvas, #8B5CF6 brand purple, #06B6D4 cyan, #F59E0B gold) protects dark-adapted eyes in laser spectroscopy rooms and low-light laboratory environments.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 2 -->
<h2>2. Installation & Quick Setup</h2>
<p>
  ChemBuddy is distributed as an optimized Android APK and standalone cross-platform package.
</p>

<h3>Installation Steps</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Download Release APK:</strong> Obtain <code>ChemBuddy-v3.5.0-by-Prajwal-A-Kambar.apk</code> from the official GitHub Releases page.</li>
  <li><strong>Enable Unknown Sources:</strong> On your Android device, navigate to <em>Settings → Security → Install Unknown Apps</em> and allow your browser or file manager.</li>
  <li><strong>Install APK:</strong> Open the downloaded APK file and tap <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Grant Permissions:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> Required for the 8:30 AM Timetable Briefing, 30-minute advance class reminders, and 8:00 PM Daily Psychology Facts.</li>
      <li><strong>Exact Alarms (Android 12+):</strong> Ensures class alerts fire with pinpoint accuracy down to the minute.</li>
      <li><strong>Storage / Media:</strong> Required if you wish to import university timetable PDFs or study notes into the PDF Library.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Initial Profile Setup:</strong> On first launch, enter your Name, University/College (e.g., Bangalore City University), Semester (1 to 4), and Specialization (Organic, Inorganic, Physical, or Analytical Chemistry).</li>
</ol>

<!-- CHAPTER 3 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>3. Smart Timetable & Attendance Intelligence Engine</h2>
<p>
  The attendance module in ChemBuddy is not a simple counter—it is a predictive mathematical engine designed to prevent hall ticket debarment and manage attendance safely.
</p>

<h3>The 75% Cutoff Mathematics</h3>
<p>
  Most Indian and global universities enforce a mandatory <strong>75% attendance threshold</strong> for semester exam eligibility. ChemBuddy constantly computes two critical metrics:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Classes Needed to Reach 75% (Target Equation):</strong>
    <p>If current attendance is below 75%, ChemBuddy solves:</p>
    <p><code>$$	ext{Needed} = \max\left(0, \lceil 3 	imes 	ext{Absent} - 	ext{Present} ceilight)$$</code></p>
    <p>It tells you the exact number of consecutive classes you must attend without missing a single one to recover eligibility.</p>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Safe Bunks Available (Buffer Equation):</strong>
    <p>If current attendance is safely above 75%, ChemBuddy solves:</p>
    <p><code>$$	ext{Can Skip} = \max\left(0, \lfloor (	ext{Present} - 3 	imes 	ext{Absent}) / 3 flooright)$$</code></p>
    <p>This reveals the exact number of classes you can afford to skip while remaining strictly above the 75.0% threshold.</p>
  </li>
</ol>

<h3>Postponed, Cancelled & Excused Classes</h3>
<p>
  ChemBuddy supports four distinct attendance states:
</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th>Effect on Percentage</th>
      <th>Use Case</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Present (✅)</strong></td>
      <td>Increments both Present and Total Count</td>
      <td>Student attended the class in person or online.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Absent (❌)</strong></td>
      <td>Increments Total Count, Present remains unchanged</td>
      <td>Student missed class or arrived after roll call.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Postponed / Cancelled (⏸️)</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Excluded from calculation</strong></td>
      <td>Faculty was absent, college holiday, or lab rescheduled. Does not penalize student.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Excused / On Duty (OD)</strong></td>
      <td>Treated as Present</td>
      <td>Official college duty, conference, sports, or medical leave approved by HOD.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>2D University Grid Timetable Parser</h3>
<p>
  Instead of manually typing weekly classes, you can load institutional schedules directly:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Auto-Extraction:</strong> Parses complex university timetable tables (including Dr. Manmohan Singh BCU MSc Chemistry presets).</li>
  <li><strong>Combined Practical Codes:</strong> Automatically recognizes 4-hour joint lab sessions (e.g. <code>CHE-504P</code> Organic Lab).</li>
  <li><strong>Faculty Legend Resolution:</strong> Maps faculty acronyms (e.g. <code>DS</code> → <em>Dr. Sharma</em>) to schedule slots automatically.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 4 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>4. Notification System & Action Shade (1-Tap Attendance)</h2>
<p>
  ChemBuddy features an active notification engine anchored to the <strong>Asia/Kolkata (IST)</strong> timezone, operating across 5 dedicated Android channels.
</p>

<div class="callout callout-success">
  <div class="callout-title">⚡ Industry-First: Action Shade Attendance</div>
  You never have to open the app to mark attendance! When a class reminder arrives in your notification shade, tap <strong>Present ✅</strong> or <strong>Absent ❌</strong> directly from the notification. ChemBuddy instantly logs the record to local Hive storage, updates your percentages, and posts a discreet confirmation toast.
</div>

<h3>The 5 Notification Channels</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Channel Name</th>
      <th>Trigger Time</th>
      <th>Description & Purpose</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Class Reminders</strong><br><code>chem_buddy_classes</code></td>
      <td>30 min before class (customizable: 5, 10, 15, 30, 60m)</td>
      <td>Advance alert with room number, subject, attendance health tier, and direct 1-tap Present / Absent action buttons.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Daily Timetable</strong><br><code>chem_buddy_daily</code></td>
      <td>Every morning at <strong>8:30 AM sharp</strong></td>
      <td>Complete morning briefing: class count, time breakdown, rooms, overall attendance %, and humorous chemistry banter.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Daily Psychology Facts</strong><br><code>chem_buddy_psychology_facts</code></td>
      <td>Every evening at <strong>8:00 PM sharp</strong></td>
      <td>Daily fascinating insight into human behavior, memory, cognitive biases, or habits (120+ rotating facts).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Tests & Assignments</strong><br><code>chem_buddy_deadlines</code></td>
      <td>24h & 2h before deadline</td>
      <td>Reminders for upcoming internal assessments, lab record submissions, seminars, and university exams.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Study & Flashcards</strong><br><code>chem_buddy_flashcards</code></td>
      <td>When spaced review is due</td>
      <td>Active recall reminders preventing memory decay along the Ebbinghaus forgetting curve.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- CHAPTER 5 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>5. Daily Psychology Facts Engine (120+ Curated Facts)</h2>
<p>
  Inspired by the popular "Psychology Facts" app, ChemBuddy v3.5.0 includes a dedicated, scientifically grounded psychology facts engine. Studying postgraduate chemistry demands deep focus, high emotional resilience, and optimized memory retention. This feature delivers daily evidence-based cognitive insights.
</p>

<h3>Domains of Psychology Covered</h3>
<div class="feature-grid">
  <div class="feature-box">
    <h4>1. Cognitive Biases & Heuristics</h4>
    <p>The Zeigarnik Effect, Halo Effect, Dunning-Kruger Effect, Pratfall Effect, Spotlight Effect, Framing Effect, Anchoring Bias, Loss Aversion, Sunk Cost Fallacy, and Dual-Process Theory (System 1 vs 2).</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-box">
    <h4>2. Memory & Learning Psychology</h4>
    <p>Ebbinghaus Forgetting Curve, Testing Effect, Serial Position Effect (Primacy & Recency), State-Dependent Memory, Sleep Consolidation, Generation Effect, and Von Restorff Isolation Effect.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-box">
    <h4>3. Brain Science & Neuroplasticity</h4>
    <p>Mirror Neurons, Dopamine Anticipation Engine, Neuroplasticity Across Life, The Amygdala Hijack, The McGurk Effect, Ultradian Rhythms (90-min focus blocks), and Sleep Spindles.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-box">
    <h4>4. Habits, Focus & Peak Performance</h4>
    <p>The 20-Second Rule, Implementation Intentions ("If-Then" planning), Parkinson's Law, Decision Fatigue, The Pomodoro Effect, The 5-Second Rule, and The 1% Daily Compounding Rule.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Prime-Weighted Calendar Rotation</h3>
<p>
  To guarantee that <strong>every single day gets a completely distinct, non-repeating fact</strong>, ChemBuddy uses a deterministic prime-weighted hashing formula:
</p>
<p><code>$$	ext{Index} = \left( 	ext{Year} 	imes 365 + 	ext{DayOfYear} 	imes 47 + 	ext{Month} 	imes 13 ight) \pmod{	ext{TotalFacts}}$$</code></p>
<p>
  This ensures consecutive days never repeat and cycle across different psychological categories, while remaining completely deterministic so scheduled alarms and in-app cards display identical content.
</p>

<!-- CHAPTER 6 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>6. Home Dashboard & Contextual Intelligence</h2>
<p>
  The Home Dashboard acts as your academic mission control. It synthesizes real-time attendance, upcoming classes, diagnostic study recommendations, and daily inspiration.
</p>

<h3>Claude-Inspired Intelligent Welcome Text</h3>
<p>
  Instead of a generic "Good morning", ChemBuddy dynamically crafts 40+ chemistry-themed greetings based on three real-time parameters:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Time of Day:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><em>Midnight to 4 AM:</em> "Burning the midnight Bunsen burner, [Name] — Even catalysts need rest to regenerate."</li>
      <li><em>4 AM to 8 AM:</em> "Rise and catalyze, [Name] ⚗️ — Your neurons are fresh and ready for synthesis."</li>
      <li><em>8 AM to 12 PM:</em> "New week, new reactions. Let's start with high yield, [Name] 🔬"</li>
      <li><em>Afternoon & Evening:</em> Tailored to post-lab winding down and analytical problem solving.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Attendance Health Tiers:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><em>Below 75% (Danger):</em> "Your attendance needs an emergency titration, [Name] ⚠️ Every class counts today."</li>
      <li><em>85%+ (Exemplary):</em> "Look at you, academic weapon! Flawless attendance streak intact 🌟"</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Day of the Week:</strong> Special Monday kickoff energy and Friday sprint reflections.</li>
</ol>

<h3>In-App Daily Psychology Fact Card</h3>
<p>
  Located directly in the dashboard between the MSc Chemistry Hub and Schedule status:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Category Chip:</strong> Color-coded badge (e.g., Purple for <em>Cognitive Biases</em>, Blue for <em>Memory</em>, Green for <em>Habits</em>).</li>
  <li><strong>Title & Emoji:</strong> Clearly formatted concept name (e.g. <code>⏳ The Zeigarnik Effect</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Detailed Phenomenon:</strong> 2–3 sentences explaining the underlying psychological discovery.</li>
  <li><strong>Practical Takeaway Box:</strong> <code>💡 Insight:</code> Actionable advice tailored for studying and daily life.</li>
  <li><strong>Shuffle Button (🔀):</strong> Tap to cycle through random facts on demand for quick mental breaks.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 7 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>7. ChemDraw Pro & Ketcher Pro (118-Element Molecular Sketcher)</h2>
<p>
  ChemBuddy v3.5.0 features a full-fledged chemical structure drawing canvas optimized for touchscreens and desktop mice alike.
</p>

<h3>118-Element Periodic Table Modal</h3>
<p>
  Tap the element button or the <code>🧪</code> icon to open the complete 118-element IUPAC periodic table:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Instant Search:</strong> Filter elements by symbol (<code>Fe</code>), name (<code>Iron</code>), or atomic number (<code>26</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Category Filters:</strong> Filter by Alkali metals, Alkaline earth, Transition metals, Lanthanides, Actinides, Post-transition, Metalloids, Nonmetals, Halogens, and Noble gases.</li>
  <li><strong>Full CPK Color Palette:</strong> Every element renders with standard CPK colors (Carbon: dark grey, Oxygen: red, Nitrogen: blue, Chlorine: green, Bromine: dark red, etc.).</li>
</ul>

<h3>ChemDraw Pro Canvas Tools</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Tool / Icon</th>
      <th>Tool Name</th>
      <th>Operation & Function</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>— / = / ≡</strong></td>
      <td>Bonds</td>
      <td>Draws single, double, or triple covalent bonds between atoms with automatic angle snapping (30°/60°/120°).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>▲ / ▰</strong></td>
      <td>Stereo Bonds</td>
      <td>Wedge (solid) and Dash (hashed) bonds for indicating R/S stereochemistry and 3D spatial orientation.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>⤴</strong></td>
      <td>Electron Arrow</td>
      <td>Curved arrow for arrow-pushing mechanisms (nucleophilic attack, resonance, pericyclic electron flow).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>⬚</strong></td>
      <td>Marquee Selection</td>
      <td>Drag a selection rectangle over atoms to group, move, rotate, or delete fragments collectively.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>🧹</strong></td>
      <td>2D Clean-Up</td>
      <td>Standardizes all bond lengths to 55px and snaps valence angles to idealized textbook geometry.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>+ / -</strong></td>
      <td>Formal Charges</td>
      <td>Applies +1, -1, +2, -2 formal charge badges with circled superscripts and exports <code>M CHG</code> in MDL Molfiles.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>→</strong></td>
      <td>Reaction Arrow</td>
      <td>Draws a horizontal reaction arrow separating reactants from products on the canvas.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>🔍</strong></td>
      <td>Pinch & Pan</td>
      <td>Two-finger pinch to zoom (0.3x to 3.0x) and two-finger drag to pan canvas. Tap 🔍 to reset view to 1.0x.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Functional Group Quick Palette</h3>
<p>
  Quickly attach standard functional groups to any selected atom in one tap:
</p>
<p><code>—OH</code> (Hydroxyl) · <code>—NH₂</code> (Amino) · <code>—COOH</code> (Carboxylic Acid) · <code>—CHO</code> (Aldehyde) · <code>—NO₂</code> (Nitro) · <code>—CN</code> (Cyano)</p>

<h3>MSc Molecular Templates</h3>
<p>
  Non-destructive template loading allows adding rings and heterocycles without overwriting your existing sketch:
  <strong>Benzene</strong>, <strong>Cyclohexane</strong>, <strong>Cyclopentane</strong>, <strong>Pyridine</strong>, <strong>Aspirin</strong>, <strong>Naphthalene</strong>, <strong>Indole</strong>, <strong>Imidazole</strong>, <strong>Thiophene</strong>, <strong>Furan</strong>, <strong>18-Crown-6</strong>, <strong>Ferrocene</strong>, <strong>Steroid core</strong>, <strong>Boc/Fmoc/TBS protecting groups</strong>, and <strong>Porphyrin ring</strong>.
</p>

<!-- CHAPTER 8 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>8. Reaction Product Prediction & 2D Vector SVG Output</h2>
<p>
  A major breakthrough in ChemBuddy v3.5.0 is the complete overhaul of chemical reaction product prediction and its vector graphics output.
</p>

<h3>45+ Instant Offline Reaction Rules (0ms Latency)</h3>
<p>
  When you draw reactants or enter reactant SMILES and tap <strong>Predict Product ⚡</strong>, ChemBuddy first runs its deterministic offline reaction engine:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Aspirin Synthesis:</strong> Salicylic Acid + Acetic Anhydride $ightarrow$ Aspirin + Acetic Acid.</li>
  <li><strong>Paracetamol Synthesis:</strong> 4-Aminophenol + Acetic Anhydride $ightarrow$ Paracetamol.</li>
  <li><strong>Acetanilide Synthesis:</strong> Aniline + Acetic Anhydride $ightarrow$ Acetanilide.</li>
  <li><strong>Esterification:</strong> Benzoic Acid / Carboxylic acids + Alcohols $ightarrow$ Esters (Methyl benzoate, Ethyl benzoate, Ethyl acetate).</li>
  <li><strong>Electrophilic Aromatic Substitution (EAS):</strong> Nitration, Bromination, Sulfonation, Friedel-Crafts Alkylation & Acylation of Benzene, Toluene, Aniline, and Phenol.</li>
  <li><strong>Named Organic Reactions:</strong> Kolbe-Schmitt, Reimer-Tiemann, Williamson Ether Synthesis, Aldol Condensation, Cannizzaro, Benzoin, Diels-Alder cycloadditions.</li>
  <li><strong>Additions & Eliminations:</strong> Markovnikov & Anti-Markovnikov additions to alkenes, SN1/SN2 substitutions, E1/E2 eliminations, carbonyl reductions (NaBH4/LiAlH4), and alcohol oxidations.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Pure Client-Side 2D Vector SVG Engine (<code>SmilesSvgGenerator</code>)</h3>
<p>
  Previously, chemical structure renderers either relied on external server calls (like NIH Cactus) or fell back to raw text placeholders (<code>&lt;text&gt;PRODUCT&lt;/text&gt;</code>). ChemBuddy v3.5.0 introduces a standalone, client-side SVG generator:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Hand-Tuned Textbook Coordinates:</strong> High-precision coordinates for all common aromatic and heterocyclic scaffolds ensure publication-quality geometry.</li>
  <li><strong>Graph-Based Layout Engine:</strong> Arbitrary SMILES strings are parsed into molecular graphs with regular polygon rings (5, 6-membered), 120° zig-zag aliphatic chains, and double/triple bond offsets.</li>
  <li><strong>CPK Heteroatoms & Masks:</strong> Heteroatoms (O: red, N: blue, S: yellow, P: orange, Halogens: green/brown/purple) render with circular background masks to cleanly occlude underlying bonds.</li>
  <li><strong>100% Vector Scalability:</strong> The resulting SVGs render sharply at any zoom scale or DPI without pixelation.</li>
</ol>

<!-- CHAPTER 9 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>9. Spectroscopy & Chromatography Hub</h2>
<p>
  The Spectroscopy Hub covers 8 essential analytical techniques taught across postgraduate chemistry curricula.
</p>

<h3>The 8 Analytical Techniques</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Reverse-Phase HPLC (Chromatography):</strong> Retention factor ($k'$), resolution ($R_s$), theoretical plates ($N$), and tailing factor ($T_f$).</li>
  <li><strong>Gas Chromatography (Chromatography):</strong> Kovats retention index ($I$), Van Deemter equation ($H = A + B/u + Cu$).</li>
  <li><strong>Thin Layer Chromatography (Chromatography):</strong> Retention factor ($R_f = d_{	ext{solute}} / d_{	ext{solvent}}$).</li>
  <li><strong>500 MHz 1H NMR (Spectroscopy):</strong> Chemical shifts ($\delta$, ppm), spin-spin coupling ($J$, Hz), integration, and splitting patterns.</li>
  <li><strong>13C DEPT NMR (Spectroscopy):</strong> Quaternary carbons, CH, CH2, and CH3 discrimination across DEPT-45, DEPT-90, and DEPT-135.</li>
  <li><strong>FT-IR Spectroscopy (Spectroscopy):</strong> Functional group frequencies ($ar{
u}$, $	ext{cm}^{-1}$), Hooke's law, reduced mass ($\mu$).</li>
  <li><strong>Mass Spectrometry (Spectroscopy):</strong> Molecular ion ($M^+$), base peak, isotope clusters ($M+1$, $M+2$), and Nitrogen Rule.</li>
  <li><strong>UV-Visible Spectroscopy (Spectroscopy):</strong> Beer-Lambert law ($A = arepsilon c l$), $\lambda_{\max}$, chromophores, and auxochromes.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Interactive Zoom & Peak Inspection</h3>
<p>
  Every technique includes a high-resolution interactive spectrogram:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Pinch & Pan (1.0x to 5.0x):</strong> Smooth 2D navigation powered by <code>InteractiveViewer</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Zoom Toolbar:</strong> Dedicated on-screen buttons: <code>+</code> (Zoom in), <code>-</code> (Zoom out), <code>Reset</code> (1.0x), and live zoom level badge.</li>
  <li><strong>Haptic Peak Snapping:</strong> Tap near any peak on the spectrum to trigger haptic feedback, snapping an inspection crosshair that displays exact chemical shift ($\delta$), retention time ($t_R$), or wavenumber ($	ext{cm}^{-1}$).</li>
  <li><strong>Textbook KaTeX Math:</strong> All fundamental principles, formulas, and axis definitions render with beautiful KaTeX equations.</li>
</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 10 -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>10. Spectroscopy Structure Solver Intelligence (52+ Molecules)</h2>
<p>
  The Structure Solver is an algorithmic and database-driven deduction engine that solves unknown molecular structures from multi-spectral data.
</p>

<h3>52+ Curated MSc Chemistry Compounds</h3>
<p>
  Contains full spectral fingerprints ($^1	ext{H}$ NMR, $^{13}	ext{C}$ NMR, FT-IR, MS, UV-Vis) for over 52 postgraduate benchmark molecules:
  <em>Aspirin, Paracetamol, Benzoic Acid, Salicylic Acid, Benzaldehyde, Phenol, Aniline, Nitrobenzene, Toluene, Benzyl Alcohol, Acetophenone, Benzocaine, 1-Bromopropane, 2-Bromopropane, Vanillin, Ethyl propionate, Methyl salicylate, Ibuprofen, Pyridine, etc.</em>
</p>

<h3>Algorithmic Solver Workflow for Arbitrary Formulas</h3>
<p>
  When presented with an unlisted molecular formula (e.g. $C_8H_8O$), the solver executes a 4-step deduction:
</p>
<div class="step-box">
  <p><span class="step-num">1</span> <strong>Double Bond Equivalent (DBE / IHD):</strong></p>
  <p><code>$$	ext{DBE} = C + 1 - rac{H}{2} - rac{X}{2} + rac{N}{2}$$</code></p>
  <p>A DBE of 4+ immediately signals a benzene ring ($C_6H_5$ or substituted).</p>
</div>
<div class="step-box">
  <p><span class="step-num">2</span> <strong>FT-IR Functional Group Classification:</strong></p>
  <p>Cross-references carbonyls ($1680	ext{–}1750	ext{ cm}^{-1}$), hydroxyls ($3200	ext{–}3600	ext{ cm}^{-1}$), and aromatic C=C stretches ($1500	ext{–}1600	ext{ cm}^{-1}$).</p>
</div>
<div class="step-box">
  <p><span class="step-num">3</span> <strong>1H NMR Splitting & Integration Analysis:</strong></p>
  <p>Distinguishes isomers (e.g. Acetophenone's 3H singlet at $\delta 2.6$ vs Benzaldehyde's 1H singlet at $\delta 9.9$).</p>
</div>
<div class="step-box">
  <p><span class="step-num">4</span> <strong>Constitutional Isomer Ruling-Out:</strong></p>
  <p>Explains systematically why other constitutional isomers with the same formula are impossible based on the observed data.</p>
</div>

