</ul>

<!-- CHAPTER 17 -->
<h2>17. Troubleshooting & Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q1: Why didn't my 8:30 AM timetable notification sound?</div>
  <strong>Answer:</strong> On Android 12+, ensure that <em>"Alarms & Reminders"</em> permission is granted in Android System Settings. Also, check that battery optimization for ChemBuddy is set to <em>"Unrestricted"</em> so Android's Doze mode does not defer morning alarms.
</div>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q2: Can I draw inorganic coordination complexes in ChemDraw Pro?</div>
  <strong>Answer:</strong> Yes! Open the 118-element periodic table, select your central transition metal (e.g. Fe, Co, Pt), and use coordination bonds. You can also load the <em>Ferrocene</em> or <em>Porphyrin</em> templates directly.
</div>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q3: How does ChemBuddy calculate attendance if a class is cancelled?</div>
  <strong>Answer:</strong> Mark the class as <em>Postponed / Cancelled (⏸️)</em>. ChemBuddy completely removes that slot from both the numerator and denominator, ensuring your percentage is never unfairly penalized.
</div>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
  <div class="callout-title">Q4: Does the reaction product predictor require internet?</div>
  <strong>Answer:</strong> No! The 45+ standard MSc organic reaction rules and the <code>SmilesSvgGenerator</code> vector engine run 100% locally on your device with 0ms latency.
</div>

